==English==

===Etymology===
Named after [[w:Hans Asperger|Hans Asperger]] + {{term|syndrome}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈæs.pɜː.dʒɜz ˈsɪn.dɹəʊm/}}
* {{audio|en-uk-Asperger's syndrome.ogg|Audio (UK)}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈæsˌp˭ɹ̩ɡɹ̩z ˈsɪndɹoʊm/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=Asperger’s [[syndrome]]|s|-}}

# {{uncountable|neurology}} An [[autism]]-related [[developmental]] [[disorder]] characterised by sustained impairment in [[social]] [[interaction]] and [[nonverbal]] [[communication]] and by restricted, repetitive, pedantic and stereotyped activities, interests, speech and routines.
# {{countable}} A person diagnosed with Asperger's syndrome.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|syndrome}} [[AS]], [[Aspie]]
* {{sense|person diagnosed with syndrome}} [[Aspie]]

====See also====
* [[autism]]
* [[learning disability]]
* [[PDD]]
* [[pervasive developmental disorder]]

